    "result_text": "Done. BUILD SUCCESS with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the code-generation step now:\n- Prefixes `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of `city`.\n- Keeps `LAST3` = upper-cased first three of `lastName`.\n- Computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** sequence: one more than the owners already in that city (matched case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace, the same normalization the other assign steps use), instead of the previous global count.\n- Extracted a shared `prefix3(...)` helper for the city/last-name prefixes.\n\n**Values derived from `customerCode`** \u2014 the `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper.java` interpolates `owner.getCustomerCode()` directly (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`); no code change was needed there.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` description/example (`LON-SMI-0007`) and the `membershipNumber` example (`LON-SMI-0007-M26`) to match the new format.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting the code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
